{"id":"b12","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":10,"of":22,"title":"Half past four","titleHe":"מָה הַשָּׁעָה","goal":"Tell the time — the one thing the feminine numbers are needed for daily.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"You have the word שָׁעָה and you have both sets of numbers. What is missing is that the hour is feminine, so a clock runs entirely on the set the counting lesson listed but never gave you as words — the set you also use counting out loud with nothing in front of you. Here they are."},{"type":"table","caption":"Reading a clock","head":["time","literally","Hebrew"],"rows":[["1:00 — one o'clock","hour one","שָׁעָה אַחַת"],["2:15 — a quarter past two","two and a quarter","שְׁתַּיִם וָרֶבַע"],["3:30 — half past three","three and a half","שָׁלוֹשׁ וָחֵצִי"],["4:20 — twenty past four","four and twenty","אַרְבַּע וְעֶשְׂרִים"],["4:45 — a quarter to five","a quarter to five","רֶבַע לְחָמֵשׁ"],["5:50 — ten to six","ten to six","עֲשָׂרָה לְשֵׁשׁ"]]},{"type":"text","body":"Past the half hour you count down to the next hour with לְ, exactly as English does — and the minutes in that countdown switch to the masculine numbers, because what is being counted there is דַּקּוֹת left out of the sentence."},{"type":"tip","body":"וָ, and, is what joins the hour to its minutes: שְׁתַּיִם וָרֶבַע. To say at an hour, use בְּ — בְּשֶׁבַע, at seven; and for a round hour in writing, בְּשָׁעָה שֶׁבַע."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"מָה הַשָּׁעָה?","en":"What time is it?"},{"he":"הַשָּׁעָה שְׁמוֹנֶה וָרֶבַע.","en":"It's a quarter past eight."},{"he":"אֲנִי בָּא בְּשֶׁבַע וָחֵצִי.","en":"I'm coming at half past seven."},{"he":"עוֹד חָמֵשׁ דַּקּוֹת.","en":"Five more minutes."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אַחַת","en":"one (f.)","translit":"achat"},{"he":"שְׁתַּיִם","en":"two (f.)","translit":"shtayim"},{"he":"שָׁלוֹשׁ","en":"three (f.)","translit":"shalosh"},{"he":"אַרְבַּע","en":"four (f.)","translit":"arba"},{"he":"חָמֵשׁ","en":"five (f.)","translit":"chamesh"},{"he":"שֵׁשׁ","en":"six (f.)","translit":"shesh"},{"he":"שֶׁבַע","en":"seven (f.)","translit":"sheva"},{"he":"שְׁמוֹנֶה","en":"eight (f.)","translit":"shmone"},{"he":"תֵּשַׁע","en":"nine (f.)","translit":"tesha"},{"he":"עֶשֶׂר","en":"ten (f.)","translit":"eser"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["seems, looks","ram's horn","known","one (f.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אַחַת","translit":"achat"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["that is to say (כלומר)","asks","bedroom","two (f.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שְׁתַּיִם","translit":"shtayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["three (f.)","how are you (f.)","thank you","next to"],"correct":0,"prompt":"שָׁלוֹשׁ","translit":"shalosh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["story","an oath","four (f.)","cheap"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אַרְבַּע","translit":"arba"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["outside","five (f.)","houses","spoil, plunder"],"correct":1,"prompt":"חָמֵשׁ","translit":"chamesh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["cucumber","a net, a network","seventy","six (f.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שֵׁשׁ","translit":"shesh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["girl","seven (f.)","window","from"],"correct":1,"prompt":"שֶׁבַע","translit":"sheva"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “two (f.)”?","options":["בְּשֶׁקֶט","שְׁתַּיִם","מְחַפֵּשׂ","מְכוֹנִית"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Reading a clock — ten to six?","options":["שָׁלוֹשׁ וָחֵצִי","עֲשָׂרָה לְשֵׁשׁ","שְׁתַּיִם וָרֶבַע","שָׁעָה אַחַת"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"חָמֵשׁ","translit":"chamesh","en":"five (f.)"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["עֶשֶׂר","שְׁתַּיִם","אַחַת","תֵּשַׁע"],"correct":1,"say":"שְׁתַּיִם","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Reading a clock — half past three?","options":["שָׁעָה אַחַת","שָׁלוֹשׁ וָחֵצִי","אַרְבַּע וְעֶשְׂרִים","שְׁתַּיִם וָרֶבַע"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “six (f.)”?","options":["מַחֲשָׁבָה","שֵׁשׁ","יוֹמַיִם","חָתוּל"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Reading a clock — one o'clock?","options":["שָׁעָה אַחַת","שְׁתַּיִם וָרֶבַע","שָׁלוֹשׁ וָחֵצִי","אַרְבַּע וְעֶשְׂרִים"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"עוֹד חָמֵשׁ ___.","en":"Five more minutes.","options":["דַּקּוֹת","אַרְבַּע","חָמֵשׁ","אַחַת"],"correct":0,"full":"עוֹד חָמֵשׁ דַּקּוֹת."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “ten (f.)” in Hebrew","answer":"עֶשֶׂר","hint":"eser"}]}